    title: "Why is Selena Gomez being sued?",
    summary: "BBC journalist Ana Guerra-Moore looks at why investors who backed Wondermind Global are claiming the pop star failed to fulfil promises.",
    preview: "Selena Gomez is being sued by five investors in her mental health company, Wondermind Global. The Hollywood actress and pop star founded the company with her mother five years ago, but now investors are claiming her 'abject dereliction of duties' has left the company in a 'state of financial difficulty'. The lawsuit will try to recover $1.2m (£890,00) it claims it was invested as well as costs and damages. The BBC has contacted Wondermind and Gomez's representatives for comment.",
    body: "Selena Gomez is being sued by five investors in her mental health company, Wondermind Global.\n\nThe Hollywood actress and pop star founded the company with her mother five years ago, but now investors are claiming her 'abject dereliction of duties' has left the company in a 'state of financial difficulty'.\n\nThe lawsuit will try to recover $1.2m (£890,00) it claims it was invested as well as costs and damages.\n\nThe BBC has contacted Wondermind and Gomez's representatives for comment.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- Selena GomezUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- CultureUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
